<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  PRODUCT-level overlay. This directory exists for exactly one reason: to beat
  vendor/lineage's own product overlay, which device/itel/S666LN/overlay/ cannot.

  WHY A SECOND OVERLAY DIRECTORY
    build/make/core/package_internal.mk:154,158,175
        static_resource_overlays := $(product_package_overlays) $(device_package_overlays)
        LOCAL_RESOURCE_DIR       := $(static_resource_overlays) $(LOCAL_RESOURCE_DIR)
        # In aapt2 the last takes precedence.
        my_resource_dirs         := $(call reverse-list,$(LOCAL_RESOURCE_DIR))
    The list is REVERSED before aapt2 sees it, so the EARLIEST entry wins.
    PRODUCT_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS therefore beats DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS, always.
    device.mk's overlay/ is a DEVICE overlay, so it loses to
    vendor/lineage/overlay/common no matter what it contains — which is why the
    build-77 attempt at the string below shipped DEAD and was retracted (5cd3863).
    Ordering within the product list is safe: lineage_S666LN.mk inherits
    device.mk (line 44) BEFORE vendor/lineage/config/common_full_phone.mk
    (line 47), so this directory is appended first and wins the reverse.
-->
<resources>

    <!-- The DeviceConfig "configurator" role.

         WRITE_DEVICE_CONFIG is protectionLevel="signature|verifier|configurator"
         and NOT `privileged`, so no privapp allowlist can grant it (build 73
         shipped one; it was inert and is deleted). The only grant path is:
             PermissionManagerServiceImpl:3525  bp.isConfigurator() &&
                 getKnownPackageNames(PACKAGE_CONFIGURATOR) contains pkg
             PackageManagerService:2060         R.string.config_deviceConfiguratorPackageName

         AOSP ships this EMPTY (core/res/.../config.xml:3400) and crDroid
         overlays it to its own bundled org.protonaosp.deviceconfig.

         OPERATOR DECISION 2026-08-25 — give it to GMS. The reasoning is about
         which BUILD this is, not about Google:
           an empty/proton configurator is correct for a VANILLA build, because
           that build is meant to be flashed with microG later. THIS IS A GAPPS
           BUILD — MindTheGapps is baked in (apply-overlays-v2.sh step 12) and
           the device carries com.google.android.gms + gsf. The role belongs to
           whichever flag system is ACTUALLY IN USE, so here that is GMS.
           Leaving it on the Proton app is the wrong owner, not a neutral default.

         ⚠ THIS IS EITHER/OR. The role is a single string, so setting it here
         TAKES it from org.protonaosp.deviceconfig, which is bundled and stays
         installed. That trade is accepted deliberately, not overlooked.

         ⚠ VERIFY BY VALUE, NEVER BY PRESENCE. A resource NAME is in
         framework-res whether or not anyone sets it, so grepping resources.arsc
         proves nothing — that is how build 77's dead override looked correct.
         The check is:
             aapt2 dump resources <SHIPPED framework-res.apk> |
                 grep -A2 config_deviceConfiguratorPackageName
         and on the device:
             dumpsys package com.google.android.gms | grep WRITE_DEVICE_CONFIG
                 -> granted=true, and the ~166/boot SecurityExceptions go to 0. -->
    <string name="config_deviceConfiguratorPackageName" translatable="false">com.google.android.gms</string>

</resources>
